LRC IN THE 2-ADIC COLUMN-FAMILY MODES
================================================================================================
n = 2^r * odd.  Odd roots move by x+2; columns move by x*2.
Tournament blowup is the row step.  Mode-B/add-two is the top-row column step.

BOUNDARY UNIT DEBT ALONG x*2 CHAINS
================================================================================================
For initial segments, boundary debt = phi(n).  The first doubling is the seam.

  odd  n-chain              phi-chain            phi-ratios      phi/n-chain
  3   3 -> 6 -> 12         2 -> 2 -> 4          1 -> 2          2/3 -> 1/3 -> 1/3
  5   5 -> 10              4 -> 4               1               4/5 -> 2/5
  7   7 -> 14              6 -> 6               1               6/7 -> 3/7
  9   9 -> 18              6 -> 6               1               2/3 -> 1/3

ODD ROOT x+2 CHAIN, FIRST EVEN CHILDREN 2*x
================================================================================================
This is the LRC analogue of top-row column motion followed by first blowup.

  odd  child n  lpd  skip  gap/th      debt   product   BT_2     BT_odd
  3         6    3     2       1/20      12       3/5        9        4
  5        10    5     4       1/56      48       6/7       34     48/5
  7        14    7     6      5/924      84      5/11       66       12
  9        18    9     8      1/176     176         1      116   496/27

DESIGNED QUOTIENT-LADDER ROW MODE n -> 2n
================================================================================================
Compare designed largest-proper-divisor ladders inside each odd-root column.

  odd  pair        gap ratio  debt ratio  product ratio  BT2 ratio  note
  1    4->8         6/35           4          24/35        3/2  frontier tax
  1    8->16      35/132        35/6       1225/792      35/12  frontier tax
  3    6->12       15/22        10/3          25/11      65/36  frontier tax
  9    9->18      21/176       88/15           7/10      58/15  first-blowup seam

SMALLEST DESIGNED FIRST-EVEN LADDERS BY VISIBLE GAP
================================================================================================
  rank  n   odd  gap/th      debt   product   interpretation
     1  14     7      5/924      84      5/11  first even child of 7
     2  18     9      1/176     176         1  first even child of 9
     3  10     5       1/56      48       6/7  first even child of 5
     4   6     3       1/20      12       3/5  first even child of 3

