SYNTHESIS
================================================================================================
1. Initial LRC boundary debt has the same seam shape as tournament pairs:
   odd -> first even keeps phi fixed, then every further row step doubles it.
2. The first-even children 2*odd are the natural LRC tests for x+2 motion
   among odd roots.  n=14 and n=18 are adjacent first-even children, while
   n=16 is the pure vertical column over odd root 1.
3. Row-mode proof objects should be p-adic: external n->2n and internal
   endpoint-depth translations both move down a Bruhat-Tits cusp.
4. Column-mode proof objects should be odd-payload transfer matrices:
   changing odd root by +2 changes which product-building trees carry debt.
